List of hardware components used in this smart portable speaker:


Battery Pack: Dayton Audio LBB-3v2 (3x Samsung INR18650-30Q batteries)
BMS: 3S Battery Management System with protection
Power Switch: SPST toggle switch for main power control
DC Input Jack: 2.1mm barrel jack for 12V external power/charging
LM317 Buck Converter: 12V to 5V conversion for ESP32 system
Sure Electronics AA-JA32172: TPA3116D2 2×50W amplifier (includes built-in volume control & coupling caps)
Left/Right Speakers: 2× Dayton Audio RS100P-4 (4Ω, 30W)
Passive Radiators: 2× Dayton Audio ND105-PR
Speaker Wire: 1.5mm² (15-16 AWG) speaker wire
LM2587 Boost Converter: 5A, 9-12V to 15V (from Amazon - $8.55)
Basic Wires/Breadboard: For prototyping

ESP32-DevKitC-VE: ESP32-WROVER with 8MB Flash and PSRAM
PCM5102A I2S DAC Module: Purple board with 3.5mm jack
12V Power Adapter: Universal AC adapter (EU plug) 
Two SPH0645LM4H MEMS microphones

🔌 Additional Connections Needed:

Power Wire: 12-14 AWG for high-current boost converter to amplifier connections
Audio Cable: 3.5mm cable or RCA cable to connect DAC output to amplifier input
Heat Shrink Tubing: For wire management and strain relief

📋 Pin Connections Summary:
ESP32 to PCM5102A (I2S):

GPIO22 → LCK (Word Select)
GPIO25 → BCK (Bit Clock)
GPIO26 → DIN (Data Input)
5V → VCC, GND → GND

ESP32 to MAX9814 (Microphone):

GPIO35 (ADC1_CH7) → OUT (Analog Audio)
5V → VCC, GND → GND

Power Distribution:

12V Rail: Battery → BMS → LM2587 Boost (15V) → TPA3116D2 Amplifier
5V Rail: Battery → BMS → LM317 Buck (5V) → ESP32, PCM5102A, MAX9814
Audio Chain: ESP32 → PCM5102A → AA-JA32172 → Speakers

⚡ Power Specifications:

Battery Pack: 11.1V nominal (9V-12.6V range)
5V Rail Current: ~2A (ESP32 + audio modules)
15V Rail Current: ~5A peak (TPA3116D2 amplifier)

🎯 Project Capabilities:

Bluetooth audio streaming (A2DP from phones/computers)
WiFi connectivity for internet/cloud services
Voice processing with microphone input
LLM integration via cloud APIs
Text-to-speech and voice-to-text capabilities
2×50W stereo amplification with passive radiator bass enhancement
Battery operation with external charging capability